Revision history for Perl extension Statistics::CaseResampling.

1.01  Fri Nov 27 23:54:00 2026
  - Remove duplicate Perl definition of Statistics::CaseResampling::RdGen::CLONE_SKIP
    from CaseResampling.pm (already provided by XS in RdGen.xs.inc), fixing the
    "Subroutine ... redefined" warning under perl -w (GH #3).
  - Fix Neumaier compensated summation in cs_mean() / mean() on 32-bit x86
    (x87 extended precision, FLT_EVAL_METHOD != 0) by rounding the running sum
    to double before computing the compensation term.
  - Preserve $Config{ccflags} (e.g. -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64) when enabling strict
    warning flags in .github/workflows/ci.yml (fixes 32-bit CI binary handshake
    mismatch).

1.00  Fri Nov 27 11:45:00 2026
  - [BREAKING] Fix two-sided alpha/2 tail probabilities and Type 7 quantile
    interpolation in simple_confidence_limits_from_samples() and
    median_simple_confidence_limits() (previously used one-sided alpha
    tails and truncated 1-based indices, giving 90% CIs at confidence=0.95
    and inverted limits for confidence < 0.5).
  - [BREAKING] Use Hyndman-Fan Type 7 linear interpolation for median(),
    first_quartile(), and third_quartile() (averaging the two middle
    elements for even N in median(), median_absolute_deviation(),
    resample_medians(), and median_simple_confidence_limits()).
  - [BREAKING] Fix domain checks on normal/erf helpers:
      * Widen approx_erf_inv() from (0, 1) to its true domain (-1, 1).
      * Enforce alpha in (0, 1] in alpha_to_nsigma() and nsigma >= 0 in
        nsigma_to_alpha(), rejecting out-of-range and NaN inputs.
  - [BREAKING] Croak cleanly on empty samples in mean(), median(),
    median_absolute_deviation(), first_quartile(), third_quartile(),
    median_simple_confidence_limits(), and
    simple_confidence_limits_from_samples() instead of silently returning 0.
    (resample(), resample_medians(), and resample_means() still return [].)
  - [BREAKING] Reject undef and non-numeric elements in sample arrays and
    mean arguments instead of silently coercing them to 0.0.
  - Harden cs_select() with an introselect heapsort fallback to guarantee
    O(n log n) worst-case time on adversarial pivot sequences, and link
    explicitly against -lm in Makefile.PL.
  - Add C-accelerated resample_quantiles(), mean_percentile_confidence_limits(),
    mean_bca_confidence_limits(), and mean_studentized_confidence_limits().
  - Add Monte Carlo empirical coverage tests in t/05_coverage.t, add
    cross-platform GitHub Actions CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml), and
    update POD/README to document all 1.00 fixes and new functions.
  - Validate scalar numeric/undef parameters across all XS entrypoints,
    prevent memory leak in bca_confidence_limits_from_samples() on invalid
    jackknife elements, guard RdGen allocations against NULL/OOM, share
    implementation via ALIAS for basic/simple_confidence_limits_from_samples,
    and fix usage message typo in median_simple_confidence_limits.
  - Add LICENSE, MIN_PERL_VERSION, TEST_REQUIRES, and META_MERGE CPAN
    metadata to Makefile.PL, and add a 32-bit Perl job to CI.

0.19  Fri Nov 27 10:15:00 2026
  - Fix default PRNG seeding (previous setup(rand()) truncated to seed 0)
    by seeding from native OS entropy (BCryptGenRandom/RtlGenRandom on
    Windows, /dev/urandom on Unix) with a 32-bit-safe fallback that
    preserves $!, and automatically reseed the default RNG after fork()
    as well as ithreads CLONE.
  - Use SvUV() in RdGen::setup_array() so full unsigned 32-bit seed words
    are preserved on 32-bit-IV Perls.
  - Eliminate modulo/scaling index bias in do_resample() via Lemire's
    unbiased bounded 32-bit integer sampling.
  - Propagate NaN deterministically across all input permutations in
    cs_select() and derived order statistics, and reject NaN in
    confidence level and approx_erf_inv() domain guards.
  - Prevent signed 32-bit multiplication overflow in third_quartile() on
    very large samples.
  - Upgrade mean() to Neumaier compensated summation with overflow-safe
    incremental fallback; upgrade standard deviation functions to scaled
    single-pass summation (avoiding overflow/underflow) and allow optional
    1-argument calling form sample_standard_deviation(\@sample) and
    population_standard_deviation(\@sample).
  - Replace low-precision erf/erfinv approximations with C99 erf()/erfc()
    and Acklam + Halley normal quantile refinement for full double
    precision across extreme tails.
  - Add statistically sound, two-sided functions while preserving legacy
    functions for backward compatibility:
      * quantile() (Hyndman-Fan Type 7 in O(n) expected time)
      * percentile_confidence_limits_from_samples()
      * basic_confidence_limits_from_samples()
      * bca_confidence_limits_from_samples()
      * median_percentile_confidence_limits()
      * median_exact_confidence_limits() (exact Binomial(n, 0.5) interval)
  - Add comprehensive statistical correctness test suite in t/04_statistics.t.
  - Fix POD documentation inaccuracies and add statistical caveats.

0.18  Sun Oct 11 10:00:00 2026
  - Fix wild stack pointer deallocation (SIGABRT free() invalid pointer)
    when passing empty arrays to resampling/statistical functions (SCR-01).
  - Prevent use-after-free and double-free under ithreads by adding CLONE
    and CLONE_SKIP handlers for the PRNG state (SCR-02).
  - Fix out-of-bounds indexing in first_quartile and third_quartile for
    small samples (SCR-03).
  - Clamp confidence limit indices to valid sample bounds on extreme
    confidence levels (SCR-04).
  - Validate resample run counts (runs >= 1 && runs <= 100000000) (SCR-05).
  - Fix memory leak on invalid kth selection in select_kth (SCR-06).
  - Guard sample and population standard deviation calculations against
    division by zero on small sample sizes (SCR-07).
  - Use Perl memory allocator (Newx/Safefree) consistently in
    median_absolute_deviation (SCR-08).
  - Harden U32ArrayPtr buffer allocation and size validation (SCR-09).
  - Add comprehensive regression test suite in t/03_security.t.
  - Update author contact details to cpan@steffen-mueller.net.

0.17  Thu Jul 17 20:00:00 2025
  - Include a fallback #ifndef for what appears to be an edge case github
    actions issue.

0.16  Mon May 19 12:37:00 2025
  - Fix XS bug that made the build break under modern (stricter)
    ExtUtils::ParseXS. (Thanks Dave!)

